<footer class="notes">
  <p>Pay is total fiscal-year 2025 pay (July 2024 – June 2025): regular pay plus overtime plus other pay such as lump sums and retroactive raises. Base salary is shown beside it; a large gap usually means a one-off payout. Base salary is the annual rate at the end of the fiscal year, so it can be higher than what was actually paid when someone got a raise or started partway through the year.</p>
  <p>Source: NYC Office of Payroll Administration, <a href="https://data.cityofnewyork.us/d/k397-673e">Citywide Payroll Data (Fiscal Year)</a>. Titles share a card when their entry path is the same; appointed jobs are grouped by who appoints. A title counts once it paid at least one person $200,000 or more in total. To look up individual employees, the same payroll is searchable at <a href="https://www.seethroughny.net/payrolls/city-of-new-york" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SeeThroughNY</a>.</p>
  <p>Not affiliated with the City of New York. Requirements and links are as of October 2026; they change, so check the current exam notice or posting before applying. Job postings are cited for their requirements, and most have since closed.</p>
